Note: On CBS, due to the effect of the debut delay of '''[[Ink (TV series)|Ink]]''' on Monday, the first month of the new season on this night aired ''[[Almost Perfect]]'' at 8:30&nbsp;p.m., followed by ''CBS Wednesday Movies'' at 9 p.m. The originally planned fall Wednesday lineup took shape at the end of October with '''[[Pearl (TV series)|Pearl]]''' taking over at 8:30&nbsp;p.m., ''[[Almost Perfect]]'' moving to 9 p.m., '''[[Public Morals (1996 TV series)|Public Morals]]''' debuting at 9:30&nbsp;p.m., and '''[[EZ Streets]]''' debuting at 10 p.m. This lasted for only one week in late October. CBS cancelled Public Morals [[List of television series canceled after one episode|after it aired for only one episode]]. This meant Almost Perfect would soon be cancelled. '''[[EZ Streets]]''' would be given a 2nd chance in the spring.
